    "research": {
      "notes": "## 1. Guidance and results\n- I found no guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal in the window. The last guidance was given on the FY26 Q4 call (2026-07-29). Q1 FY27 revenue guidance is $89.85B–$90.95B, with Azure up about 45% in constant currency and capex above $50B. — 2026-07-29 — https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-earnings\n- FY26 Q4 results beat consensus: EPS $4.74 against $4.24, and revenue $90.01B against $87.61B. — 2026-07-29 — https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-earnings\n- Management said FY27 capex will grow year over year and that it expects to stay free-cash-flow positive. — 2026-07-29 — https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/events/fy-2026/earnings-fy-2026-q4\n- The next report is FY27 Q1 on 2026-10-28. — date unknown (announced) — https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/default\n- Consensus for that report is EPS of $4.71 and revenue of $90.61B. — 2026-10-12 — https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/microsoft-stock-outlook-azure-growth-and-earnings-set-to-drive-next-move-93CH-4945006\n- Another source puts revenue consensus at $90.59B. — date unknown — https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-earnings\n\n## 2. Analyst actions\n- Stifel upgraded to Buy from Hold, with the price target (PT) raised to $575 from $530. — 2026-09-23 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/msft/price-targets\n- Melius Research upgraded to Buy from Hold with a $665 PT. — date unknown (article about 9 days old) — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/microsoft-upgraded-hubspot-initiated-wall-134952467.html\n- Phillip Securities downgraded to Neutral/Hold from Accumulate, PT $515, citing the stock's re-rating. — 2026-10-12 — https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/msft-stock-gets-a-thumbs-up-from-barclays-firm-expects-quarter-to-start-showing-more-differentiation-in-software/cZxBllTRBY4\n- Yorkville Ives initiated coverage at Buy, PT $615. — 2026-10-07 — https://www.investing.com/equities/microsoft-corp-consensus-estimates\n- PT raises, per Benzinga (https://www.benzinga.com/quote/msft/price-targets):\n  - Cantor Fitzgerald, $522 to $608 — 2026-09-21\n  - Oppenheimer, $515 to $570 — 2026-09-22\n  - Piper Sandler, $550 to $610 — 2026-09-30\n  - Wells Fargo, $700 to $725 — 2026-10-01\n  - Scotiabank, $510 to $615 — 2026-10-05\n  - Evercore ISI, $528 to $635 — 2026-10-07\n- Citizens maintained Market Outperform at $550. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.benzinga.com/quote/msft/price-targets\n- Barclays raised its PT to $600 from $512 and kept Overweight. TipRanks dates this 2026-10-12 (https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msft/forecast). Yahoo dates it 2026-10-13 (https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSFT/).\n- Deutsche Bank raised its PT to $600 from $550, Buy. — 2026-10-12 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msft/forecast\n- Morgan Stanley reiterated Buy at $600. — 2026-10-12 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msft/forecast\n- J.P. Morgan reiterated Buy at $625. — 2026-10-13 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msft/forecast\n\n## 3. Litigation and regulation\n- I found no new lawsuit, fine, approval or export-control action dated in the window. These are ongoing matters that began earlier:\n  - The UK CMA opened a cloud-licensing probe. — 2026-03-31 — https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/31/microsoft-cma-investigation-uk-software-business.html\n  - A UK cloud-licensing class action was allowed to proceed. Reuters reported it as $2.8B (Yahoo copy); Courthouse News reported $2.3B. — date unknown — https://finance.yahoo.com/sectors/technology/articles/microsoft-must-face-2-8-163907031.html and https://courthousenews.com/microsoft-faces-2-3-billion-cloud-computing-lawsuit-in-uk/\n  - The FTC probe continues and reportedly widened to rivals' queries. This is a secondary source. — 2026-02 (per source) — https://tech-insider.org/microsoft-antitrust-probe-cloud-ai-2026/\n\n## 4. Customer concentration\n- I found no new customer win, loss or contract change in the window. Background:\n  - OpenAI contracted an incremental $250B of Azure services. — 2025-10-28 — https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2025/10/28/the-next-chapter-of-the-microsoft-openai-partnership/\n  - The OpenAI terms were amended: Microsoft's IP license became non-exclusive through 2032, and OpenAI can sell on other clouds. — 2026-04-27 — https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/27/openai-ends-microsoft-legal-peril-over-its-50b-amazon-deal/\n  - Anthropic committed to $30B of Azure compute. — 2025-11-18 — https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2025/11/18/microsoft-nvidia-and-anthropic-announce-strategic-partnerships/\n  - Commercial remaining performance obligations (RPO) were $678B at FY26 end, and OpenAI contracts can make this volatile quarter to quarter (aggregator). — 2026-06-30 — https://us.plus500.com/en/forecasts/microsoft-earnings-expectations\n\n## 5. Insider activity\n- No open-market purchases found.\n- CFO Amy Hood sold 41,674 shares (about $20.8M, roughly $498 average) on 2026-09-14. That is one day before the window opens; the Form 4 was filed 2026-09-15. — https://www.secform4.com/insider-trading/789019.htm\n- Hood sold another 7,305 shares (about $3.98M, $544–$547) on 2026-10-13. StockTitan tags the filing as 10b5-1. — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/MSFT/form-4-microsoft-corp-insider-trading-activity-85d38bfea1ab.html\n- Amy Coleman (chief human resources officer) had 36 shares withheld for tax. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.secform4.com/insider-trading/789019.htm\n- Before the window, CEO Nadella sold 86,525 shares under a 10b5-1 plan adopted 2026-03-08. — 2026-09-01 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/MSFT/form-4-microsoft-corp-insider-trading-activity-186dc44c42c7.html\n\n## 6. Product and competitive news\n- Microsoft launched the new Copilot app (Home, Code, Autopilot), combining chat, coding and agents. — 2026-09-25 — https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/09/25/introducing-the-new-copilot-with-home-code-and-autopilot/\n- Pricing shifts toward usage-based billing for Cowork, Code and Autopilot, and CNBC frames the launch as a response to Anthropic. — 2026-09-25 — https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/25/microsoft-copilot-ai-coding-anthropic.html\n- Fewer than 7% of more than 450M commercial Microsoft 365 seats carry Copilot licenses, per CNBC as cited by Yahoo. Microsoft reported more than 30M paid Copilot seats in July. — date unknown — https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/microsoft-relaunches-copilot-app-coding-125333413.html\n- \"Office in Copilot\" was announced. — 2026-10-09 — https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/micro",
